premise_retrieval_precision_recall_harness","routing_anti_patterns_registry","semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","spatial_world_model_counterfactual_simulation_replay","tactic_portfolio_availability_probe","target_shape_tactic_routing_gate","undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier","verifier_lab_execution_spine","verifier_lab_kernel","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":["AP-1","AP-12","AP-15"],"id":"AX-1","kind":"axiom","plain":"Formal clause: for any claim `phi` over basis `B`, admissibility requires a derivation certificate `c` and checker `K` such that `K(B,c,phi)=accept`, with `strength(phi) <= strength(K(B,c,phi))`; bare assertion has bottom evidence.","principles":["P-1","P-2"],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The game log only shows that this score can be recomputed; one matching log says nothing about the rest of the season.","maps":[{"analogy":"the number on the scoreboard","doctrine":"the claim"},{"analogy":"the plays recorded in the game log","doctrine":"the inputs the claim was computed from"},{"analogy":"adding up the plays in the game log","doctrine":"the checker that recomputes it"}],"text":"Nobody trusts a scoreboard just because it shows a number. The game log has to list the plays that add up to that score."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A page prints \"passed\" because the title of a saved result says so, and nothing recomputes the verdict from the data underneath.","does_not_prove":"A passing check limits what a claim may say; it does not make the claim true outside what that checker examined.","enforced_in_component_ids":["agent_sabotage_scheming_monitor_replay","belief_state_process_reward_replay"],"example":{"component_ids":["agent_sabotage_scheming_monitor_replay"],"text":"A replay reads a test file that declares a monitor caught an agent scheming, recomputes the verdict from the recorded trace, and rejects the run when the declared verdict does not follow from that trace."},"governs":"When a stated result may be used as evidence at all.","plain":"A result counts only when an independent check can reproduce it from the inputs it came from. A confident statement on its own counts for nothing.","potential_misread":"That a checked result is certain, when the check only limits how much the result can claim.","refuses":"Treating a written label as if it were the true result.","requires":"The inputs the claim was computed from, a certificate of how it was derived, and a checker that recomputes the verdict and accepts it.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"Answers such as \"a model said so\" or \"the record is labelled passed\" carry no weight until something independent works the answer out again."},"rests_on":[],"source_ref":"AXIOMS.md::AX-1","statement":"Formal clause: for any claim `phi` over basis `B`, admissibility requires a\nderivation certificate `c` and checker `K` such that `K(B,c,phi)=accept`, with\n`strength(phi) <= strength(K(B,c,phi))`; bare assertion has bottom evidence.\n\nLineage: Curry-Howard proof terms, proof-carrying code, verifiable computation.\n\nRoute: recorded as strongly witnessed by\n`agent_sabotage_scheming_monitor_replay`, `belief_state_process_reward_replay`,\n`evidence_truth_floor.py` and the evidence-class rows. Its negative fixtures\ndeclare a verdict that does not follow from the lower-level evidence, and the\nreplay has to catch it.\n\nAnti-axiom: a label is true because someone asserted it.","statement_sha256":"31e5bfbc333b78912a8e3f44c3010fe0d57d0a655881095be9876823671865ee","title":"Derivation before assertion","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}